ERF-CSRBoost and FixYourDataset: licence terms

This repository uses two licences for different kinds of material, plus a list of
material that is not covered by either.

1. Original source code: MIT License (Section A).
2. Original documentation, figures and result files: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
   International, CC BY 4.0 (Section B).
3. Third-party material (datasets, the published CSRBoost paper, libraries): not covered by
   Section A or B; it keeps its own terms (Section C).

If a file mixes code and prose, the MIT terms apply to the code and the CC BY 4.0 terms apply
to the prose.

No licence here adds a compulsory citation term or any other condition beyond the text of the
standard licence it names. A request to cite the work is in README.md and CITATION.cff and is a
request only.


Scope: which files fall under which licence

Section A (MIT) covers the source code written by the author:
  - backend/ (server, engine, models, tests, sample generator)
  - frontend/ (index.html and the JavaScript test files)
  - Dockerfile, fly.toml, .dockerignore, requirements.txt
  - research/scripts/ (the research runner scripts)
  - configuration files: .gitignore, .gitattributes, research/.gitignore and
    research/MANIFEST.sha256 (the list of SHA-256 values for the stored research files)

Section B (CC BY 4.0) covers the original documentation, figures and result files:
  - README.md, DEPLOY_FLY.md, THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md
  - docs/
  - samples/README.md
  - research/README.md
  - the metric-only result files in research/results/ (per-fold and per-dataset scores
    produced by the author's runs; they contain no source data)

Not covered by Section A or B (Section C):
  - samples/*.csv and any dataset file a reader downloads for research/
  - the CSRBoost paper
  - third-party libraries

CITATION.cff is metadata about this repository; it may be reused freely.


