Section C. Third-party material (not covered by Section A or B)

The following keep their own terms. Details, creators, DOIs and the changes made to the
bundled samples are in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

  - The four sample datasets in samples/ are derived from datasets of the UCI Machine Learning
    Repository, which the repository lists under CC BY 4.0. They were modified (encoding,
    subsampling, relabelling) as described in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md and samples/README.md.
    Credit and the licence belong to the original creators.

  - Dataset files used by the research runner are not part of this repository. They come from
    the UCI Machine Learning Repository and the KEEL dataset repository and remain under the
    terms of those providers. A reader downloads them from the original source.

  - The CSRBoost paper (Yadav, Joshi, Mulye, Asari, Udmale and Bhole, IEEE Access, 2025,
    DOI 10.1109/ACCESS.2025.3616207) is the copyright of its authors and publisher and is not
    redistributed here.

  - The libraries the code depends on (pandas, numpy, scikit-learn, imbalanced-learn, scipy,
    openpyxl, xlrd) are installed separately from PyPI and keep their own licences.
